1
00:00:00,221 --> 00:00:02,091
(Howard:)I wonder if only a baby
who is worthy

2
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:04,190
(Howard:)can suckle at the bosom of Thor.

3
00:00:04,192 --> 00:00:06,192
PENNY:
Okay, new salon topic.

4
00:00:06,194 --> 00:00:09,064
(Penny:)Salons-- dumb thing
from a long time ago

5
00:00:09,064 --> 00:00:12,194
(Penny:)or interesting thing made dumb
by talking about superheroes?

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,270
(Penny:)Discuss.

7
00:00:14,735 --> 00:00:17,135
(Sheldon:)I don't believe it matters
what the topic is.

8
00:00:17,139 --> 00:00:19,469
(Sheldon:)What's crucial for a salon

9
00:00:19,474 --> 00:00:20,974
(Sheldon:)is that we conduct
the discussion

10
00:00:20,976 --> 00:00:23,306
(Sheldon:)in an elevated
and insightful way.

11
00:00:23,312 --> 00:00:25,242
(Sheldon:)It's all about the execution.

12
00:00:25,247 --> 00:00:28,847
(Leonard:)Of course you'd focus on that
rather than the inspiration.

13
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:30,520
(Leonard:)Uh, new salon topic.

14
00:00:30,519 --> 00:00:33,489
(Leonard:)What's more important,
an idea or its execution?

15
00:00:33,488 --> 00:00:35,088
Oh, that's fun.

16
00:00:35,090 --> 00:00:36,720
(Sheldon:)Yeah, good for you, Leonard.

17
00:00:36,725 --> 00:00:38,255
(Sheldon:)That's a lovely little notion.

18
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:39,630
(Sheldon:)Kind of like,

19
00:00:39,628 --> 00:00:42,128
"I wish I could talk
to my uncle in Chicago."

20
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:45,200
(Sheldon:)Yeah, now stand back
while I invent the telephone.

21
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,170
"Hello? Oh, hold on."

22
00:00:47,169 --> 00:00:48,369
(Sheldon:)Leonard, it's your uncle.

23
00:00:48,370 --> 00:00:50,640
(Sheldon:)He says you just got burned.

24
00:00:51,906 --> 00:00:52,936
(Amy:)Sheldon.

25
00:00:52,941 --> 00:00:54,441
(Stuart:)You guys.
No, it's okay.

26
00:00:54,443 --> 00:00:56,743
(Leonard:)We're all adults trying to have
an intelligent discussion.

27
00:00:56,745 --> 00:00:57,915
(Leonard:)At least I am.

28
00:00:57,913 --> 00:00:59,313
(Leonard:)Howard, what
do you think?

29
00:00:59,314 --> 00:01:03,954
(Howard:)Well, I guess, as an engineer,
I lean towards execution.

